 attention to the  data rather than whether Trump praises  CEOs we are still finding about 25,000  new coronavirus cases basically every  single day so I'm  times more sometimes a little less and  deaths again have spiked yesterday  twenty-three hundred and fifty deaths in  one day in the United States a really  bad number and when you look at what's  going on in Italy when you look at  what's going on in Spain when you look  at the curves and then you see what's  going on here it's not good and  meanwhile as I told you yesterday CDC  and FEMA have a report which says they  fear that deaths might actually climb to  3,000 a day by June first with maybe  200,000 new cases a day now I hope that  doesn't happen as you all know politics  don't play a role in what I hope happens  I don't hope we have one single death  for the purpose of making Trump look bad  or helping to defeat Trump the case for  that is very clear there have been  enough deaths I don't want anyone to die  hopefully it won't happen but the  numbers in a lot of states aren't  looking good here's Donald Trump asked  yesterday in Arizona about the  coronavirus task force Trump stopped at  a Honeywell mask required factory he  refused to wear a mask I'll talk about  that later but Donald Trump again  talking about we've just done great  about everything and at one point he  Trump walked around all day yesterday  with a piece of paper in his pocket that  was just a graph of the total number of  coronavirus tests which is meaningless  right we've talked about per capita here  is Donald Trump's answer and it includes  pulling out that piece of paper when  asked about why would you now disband  the coronavirus task force everything  and don't you want to I need I just want  to say that we've done an incredible job  in testing with that being said we have  some additional including antibody tests  coming out that will even blow these  numbers away but nobody's done the job  we don't you need to continue to meet  with the task force to get this  scientific expertise  we will have certain people as an  example we have hospitals that we built  we have medical centers that we built we  have people on the task force that focus  on that we have people on the task force  that's focused exclusively on  ventilators well we have more  ventilators now than anybody in the  world and we're helping France as you  know we're helping France Italy Spain  Nigeria we're just we're giving 250 to  Nigeria we have many countries that were  helping but the ventilator problem is  also you don't need that we have now a  different it's sort of a combination of  safety and reopening so we'll have  something in a different form but the  task force for what we've done I think  everybody out there when they're being  very honest I think the job we've done  on testing will shortly be and maybe  even supersede the job that we've done  on ventilators which people can't even  believe we had a call the other day with  the governor's so it goes on for about  an additional minute but as you can tell  there's no answer there's no answer the  question was should you really end the  coronavirus task force when we are in  the middle of a pandemic and Trump says  governors are happy we have tons of  ventilators and I have a piece of paper  with a graph about testing it's striking  me as counterintuitive to end the task  force now and I want to point out one  other thing we've been watching the  numbers coming out of some of these  early openings southern states the  states that didn't have these are states  that weren't initially hotspots and they  insisted that they're good to go and  reopen the numbers aren't good look at  just one example out of Texas in Texas  cases have increased dramatically over  the last nine days Texas had 535 new  cases on April 27 that went up to 960  new cases on April 30 and that was up to  more than 1200 new cases yesterday now  understand the raw numbers are not the  important thing here the percentage  increases are if you see new cases  continue to increase in Texas at this  rate they're 34,000 cases will be more  than 50,000 cases just ten days from now  and by then if  the other northeastern and West Coast  states keep seeing declines Texas will  have dramatically more active cases than  any of these early hot spots we can do a  similar analysis in other states I hope  none of this happens but the last thing  you need right now is to end the task  force and just focus on reopening since  its that reopening which may indeed  wreak havoc in a whole bunch of states  hope it doesn't happen it's what the  data is pointing to check this out the  first 500 people who see this video and  go to david pakman.com slash skill will  get a premium membership to Skillshare  for two months completely free skill  shares the online learning community  with thousands of classes on almost  anything you can imagine always taught  by experts they have classes on drawing  painting photography video editing web  design running a small business and much  more I recently took a very interesting  class called simple productivity how to  accomplish more with less and got a  bunch of great personal productivity  tips out of it we should allow ourselves  a little time every week to either get  creative keep your brain sharp learn  something new it's great for mental  health and almost all the classes are  under an hour so it's very easy for  someone who's busy to take advantage of  it with skill share you can discover a  new passion explore something you didn't  know you would enjoy but there's also  plenty of classes for people with  experience so you can just get better at  something you're already good at and  again the first 500 people who see this  video and go to david pakman.com slash  skill will get a completely free premium  membership for two whole months giving  you access to every class Skillshare  offers check it out I put the link right  underneath this 